/coop-mega/coop-mega-molde-1516","ph":"+47 97 99 49 50"},{"n":"Moldegård post i butikk","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":62.737513,"lo":7.18301,"d":1173,"h":"Mo-Fr 08:00-22:00, Sa 08:00-20:00"},{"n":"Hurtigruta Carglass Molde","g":"essentials","k":"car_repair","la":62.738434,"lo":7.183133,"d":1188,"h":"Mo-Fr 08:00-16:00","w":"https://www.carglass.no/avdelinger/sunnmore/molde","wifi":1},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":62.737592,"lo":7.183582,"d":1202,"h":"24/7"},{"n":"Vitusapotek Molde storsenter","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":62.737759,"lo":7.184334,"d":1242,"h":"Mo-Fr 10:00-20:00, Sa 10:00-18:00","ph":"+47 71250333"},{"n":"Rema 1000 Moldegård","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":62.739227,"lo":7.185839,"d":1339,"h":"Mo-Sa 07:00-23:00","ph":"+47 71251600"},{"n":"Kongebjørka","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.740256,"lo":7.127941,"d":1672,"ds":"The Royal Birch (Norwegian: Kongebjørka) is a Norwegian national symbol and memorial of the Nazi occupation of Norway during World War II. It is located at Glomstua in the city of Molde in Møre og Romsdal, Norway. King Haakon VII and Crown Prince Olav were photographed by Per Bratland seeking shelter under the birch tree during a German bombing raid during the last weekend of April 1940.","wpu":"Kongebjørka","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Kongebjorka.jpeg/960px-Kongebjorka.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Moldemarka","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.7484,"lo":7.1261,"d":2141,"ds":"Moldemarka is a 30-square-kilometre (12 sq mi) hilly and mostly wooded recreational area north of Molde in Molde Municipality, Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. The area is known for the Molde panorama, with views of more than 222 rugged and partly snow-clad peaks, mountainous islands, green hills, and the North Atlantic Ocean to the north and west.","wpu":"Moldemarka","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Molde%2C_Norway_from_a_nearby_island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Bergmo Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.746528,"lo":7.224753,"d":3463,"ds":"Bergmo Church (Norwegian: Bergmo kirke) was a parish church of the Church of Norway in Molde Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It was located in the Bergmo area of the town of Molde, about 3.5 kilometres (2.2 mi) east of the town center. It was an annex church for the Bolsøy parish which is part of the Molde domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Bergmo Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Bergmo_sm%C3%A5kirke.jpg/960px-Bergmo_sm%C3%A5kirke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Nordbyen Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.755075,"lo":7.225627,"d":3899,"ds":"Nordbyen Church (Norwegian: Nordbyen kyrkje) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Molde Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located in the Nordbyen area of the town of Molde. It is one of the churches for the Bolsøy parish which is part of the Molde domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Nordbyen Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Nordbyen_kirke.jpg/960px-Nordbyen_kirke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Røbekk Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.752659,"lo":7.293931,"d":7038,"ds":"Røbekk Church (Norwegian: Røbekk kirke, historic: Bolsøy kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Molde Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located in the village of Røbekk, an eastern suburb of the town of Molde. It is the main church for the Bolsøy parish which is part of the Molde domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Møre.","wpu":"Røbekk Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Robekk-kirke3-Molde-Norway.jpg/960px-Robekk-kirke3-Molde-Norway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bolsøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":62.7307,"lo":7.3275,"d":8561,"ds":"Bolsøya is an island in Molde Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. The 5.2-square-kilometre (2.0 sq mi) island lies in the Romsdalsfjorden at the entrance to the Fannefjorden. The island is connected to the mainland by the Bolsøy Bridge and to the town of Molde by the Fannefjord Tunnel, both on County Road 64.","wpu":"Bolsøya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Bols%C3%B8y_gamle_kirkeg%C3%A5rd_fra_LH.jpg/960px-Bols%C3%B8y_gamle_kirkeg%C3%A5rd_fra_LH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Molde (Norwegian pronunciation: [ˈmɔ̂ɫdə] ) is a town, an Urban Area, and the seat of Molde Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. It is located in the traditional district of Romsdal. It is located on the Romsdal Peninsula, surrounding the Fannefjord and Moldefjord.","wpu":"Molde","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Downtown_Molde_%282023-10-26_11-31-23%29.jpg/960px-Downtown_Molde_%282023-10-26_11-31-23%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}